      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One bar per chromosome or scaffold, all from the same origin and drawn to its length, so the three assemblies compare by size first. Each tick is a BUSCO gene coloured by status: genome_C, the draft, is short of Complete genes and splits two chromosomes over four scaffolds. Click a bar to open that sequence and zoom along it (Ctrl or Cmd + scroll, the buttons, or shift-drag), then filter the tab to it from the detail view; switch marks, density or automatic level of detail from the toolbar, and hide a status from the legend. Input: BUSCO full tables from nf-core/genomeqc; the density below reads binned VCF counts from nf-core/sarek.\n",
